1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Hello everyone, I am Xueli. In this video, we will learn how to use some settings and functions to avoid some problems in the animation production process.

2
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Before starting today's content, please make sure you have watched our animation entry video. In that video, we briefly introduced how to make animation in Marvelous Designer and how to make your animation stable through some settings.

3
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:50,000
In this video, I used version 6.1.723. Until this version, we have fixed a lot of problems related to LNBEC files.

4
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:53,000
So I hope everyone can update to the latest version as much as possible.

5
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Next, let's take a look at the first case.

6
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,000
In this case, we can see that it has a structure similar to Hanfu.

7
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Hanfu itself is relatively loose, and many times Hanfu will have some small accessories, such as butterflies and so on.

8
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:11,000
Here we will complete the action replacement first.

9
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:16,000
First of all, I am using Hanna here, which is the virtual model built into our software.

10
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:19,000
If you need to make an action replacement,

11
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:26,000
then we now need two OBJ models to make the action replacement, because we want to use the MorphTarget function.

12
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:32,000
So let's delete the original virtual model first, and then import OBJ into the file in the upper left corner.

13
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Select an OBJ model that we have prepared before in the output menu.

14
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:41,000
Here we do not need to click on the automatic production arrangement point.

15
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Just pay attention to the unit and click OK.

16
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:54,000
After the OBJ model is imported, we adjust its surface diameter in the property menu on the right.

17
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:59,000
Because when I was making this set of Hanfu before, the surface diameter I used was 0.

18
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:03,000
So here we need to modify it at the same time.

19
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:07,000
Otherwise, it may be unstable during our second simulation.

20
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:12,000
After modifying the surface diameter to 0, we will simulate it by pressing the control key.

21
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:15,000
After the simulation, we will observe if there is any unstable place.

22
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:18,000
After there is no unstable place, we will proceed to the next step.

23
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:21,000
Then we will observe this set of clothes.

24
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:26,000
First of all, in this set of clothes, we can clearly see that there is a butterfly knot in front of it.

25
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:31,000
Although the structure of the butterfly knot is very small and the number of sheets is not very large,

26
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:37,000
it is easy to produce some instability because it has folds and layers.

27
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Especially when some movements are relatively large.

28
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:44,000
So we need to fix the knot of the butterfly knot first.

29
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:49,000
First of all, since the knot is small, it will cover most of the other sheets.

30
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:53,000
So we can reduce its particle diameter to 1.

31
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:58,000
We can reduce its particle diameter to 4 or 3 for other knots.

32
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:00,000
You don't have to worry about this.

33
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:03,000
Because the whole sheet is not a very large sheet.

34
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:06,000
So it doesn't matter if you reduce the particle diameter a little bit.

35
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:09,000
For a structure that is easy to fall like a butterfly knot,

36
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:12,000
what we need to do is to fix it with a fake sewing needle.

37
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,000
We will fix it between the two sheets.

38
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:18,000
Here we choose the fake sewing tool.

39
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:20,000
Click on the knot to the upper position.

40
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:23,000
Then click on the belt to the middle position.

41
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:28,000
When creating a fake sewing needle, try to match these two sheets with a flat state.

42
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:31,000
So that you can find the seam point more accurately.

43
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:33,000
Then open the simulation by pressing the control key.

44
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:38,000
We will see that the knot of the butterfly knot will gradually be fixed near the waist.

45
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:41,000
Here we add a fake sewing needle at the knot position.

46
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:44,000
This can prevent the whole thing from shaking up and down.

47
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:48,000
Because more intense shaking will cause the structure of the butterfly knot to fall apart.

48
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:52,000
The most common place for the butterfly knot to be sewn is near its knot.

49
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:55,000
So we first fix the knot.

50
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:59,000
Next, we can import the second OBJ file that we have prepared in advance.

51
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:01,000
Then transform it.

52
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Here we simply review how this OBJ file is extracted.

53
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:11,000
First, you need to import the model with the animation into Marvelous Designer.

54
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:14,000
Then open the animation editor at the bottom of the screen.

55
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:17,000
Then we find the first needle of this action.

56
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:22,000
In the form of the first needle, the upper left corner is redirected to the virtual model.

57
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:26,000
Of course, you can also make it in other 3D files.

58
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:32,000
It's just that we need to make sure that the face number of these two models is the same and the number of dots is the same.

59
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,000
Then we continue with the steps just now.

60
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:44,000
After selecting the second OBJ file that was extracted just now,

61
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:48,000
we switch to Morph Target in the object type column.

62
00:04:52,000 --> 00:05:00,000
After that, our system will move these two OBJ files that you have imported to point to point.

63
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:03,000
There is a transform body number at the bottom.

64
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:08,000
The more transform body numbers, the slower the calculation of this action.

65
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:10,000
The slower it is, the more stable it is.

66
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:13,000
Then we click OK to transform.

67
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:18,000
In the process of transforming, because it is moving point by point,

68
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:23,000
there may be some flatness of the human body in the process.

69
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:26,000
If the difference between the action and the action is too big,

70
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:30,000
we recommend that you best be able to find a way to make a transition in the middle.

71
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:34,000
Here we can see that in fact, in the transformation process,

72
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:39,000
we have already found some problems in the animation process of the costume.

73
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:42,000
For example, now my knot is very stable,

74
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:45,000
but if you don't fix the knot,

75
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:49,000
it may shake during this transformation process.

76
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:53,000
After the transformation is over, we can switch the view

77
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:56,000
to see if there are any other places to be changed.

78
00:05:56,000 --> 00:06:01,000
Here I found that there was a cloth that was pierced because of the movement of the finger just now.

79
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:03,000
Here we can open the simulation,

80
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:07,000
and manually drag the plate.

81
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:09,000
After dragging it out,

82
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:12,000
we can check the internal plate.

83
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:13,000
After selecting a plate,

84
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:16,000
press Shift Q to hide this plate.

85
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:17,000
Then we look at the internal plate,

86
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:19,000
see if there are any cracks or deformations.

87
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:21,000
After checking, if there is no problem,

88
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:25,000
we can press Shift W to display all the plates.

89
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:27,000
In the process of checking,

90
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:30,000
we try to look at some parts more comprehensively,

91
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:33,000
especially parts like the bottom of the page.

92
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:35,000
In the case of the heel of the foot,

93
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:37,000
because of our shoes,

94
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:38,000
generally speaking,

95
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:40,000
there are more gaps in the net.

96
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:41,000
And sometimes,

97
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:43,000
the problem of the hair line in the net

98
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:46,000
will lead to the pattern to have some Western-style problems.

99
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:48,000
So here we can first

100
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:52,000
reduce the particle diameter of the entire skirt pattern to 8.

101
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:54,000
After modifying the particle diameter,

102
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:56,000
the overall net gap will increase,

103
00:06:56,000 --> 00:07:01,000
and it is not easy to penetrate the place where the shoes are interspersed.

104
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:05,000
Then if we find that there is still a gap after reducing the particle diameter,

105
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:10,000
we can try to increase the surface diameter of the entire virtual model to 1.

106
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:13,000
Then press the control key to simulate,

107
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:18,000
let the plate and the surface diameter we just adjusted be re-closed.

108
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:20,000
Now we go back to the back,

109
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:24,000
we will find that the previous penetration problem has been solved.

110
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:26,000
Then check the knot position,

111
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:30,000
see if there is any change in the process of changing the action.

112
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:32,000
If there is no other problem,

113
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:35,000
we can start to reduce the particle diameter of the outer layer of the pattern,

114
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:37,000
and simulate it.

115
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:39,000
Because once you start recording the animation,

116
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:42,000
you can't change the particle diameter anymore.

117
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:46,000
So we have to prepare these adjustments in advance.

118
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:48,000
After adjusting the particle diameter,

119
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:53,000
we need to adjust the physical properties of the skirt pattern.

120
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:57,000
When we usually use Marvelous Designer to make Hanfu

121
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:59,000
and some dressings,

122
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:04,000
sometimes we will choose some比較有玄錘性的面料,

123
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:06,000
to make it look more intimate.

124
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:10,000
But these fabrics are often because of their own physical properties.

125
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:13,000
In the process of opening the animation simulation,

126
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:17,000
there may be an unstable or strong rebound effect.

127
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:20,000
So we need to make some adjustments to its physical properties.

128
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:25,000
First of all, here we can see that the fabric used in the skirt pattern is silk chiffon,

129
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:27,000
that is, snow-covered fabric.

130
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:28,000
Snow-covered fabric,

131
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:30,000
which has a very low particle diameter,

132
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,000
is only 0.

133
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:35,000
We need to increase the particle diameter to at least 4 or above,

134
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:39,000
in order to ensure that it can run as steadily as possible.

135
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:40,000
In addition,

136
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:43,000
because the overall properties of this pattern are all soft,

137
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:46,000
it may have a strong rebound effect

138
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:49,000
during the animation calculation or simulation process.

139
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:51,000
So at this time,

140
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:56,000
we need to increase the properties of the inner damping at the bottom of the fabric.

141
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:57,000
The inner damping properties

142
00:08:57,000 --> 00:09:00,000
affect the density of the fabric rebound.

143
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:01,000
After this number is increased,

144
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:04,000
the movement and rebound of the fabric will become slower,

145
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:09,000
as if there is resistance in the air to prevent it from rebounding.

146
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:11,000
This can help us stabilize the structure.

147
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:14,000
Secondly, we need to increase the density of the fabric,

148
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:17,000
because we have just adjusted the tension of the corner line.

149
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:19,000
So the higher the tension of the corner line,

150
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:23,000
the more difficult it is for the fabric to rotate in the direction of the corner line.

151
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:26,000
So it will sacrifice some of the rotation of the fabric.

152
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:27,000
Therefore,

153
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:29,000
we can increase the density of the fabric

154
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:33,000
to make it look more intimate and more vertical.

155
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:34,000
In addition,

156
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:35,000
increasing the density of the fabric

157
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:38,000
can also prevent the fabric from making a strong rebound.

158
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:40,000
To prevent the rebound,

159
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:43,000
it can effectively prevent the movement of the model to be too fast,

160
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:45,000
causing the fabric to follow the model,

161
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:47,000
so some shaking occurs.

162
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:50,000
Next is the setting of our belt.

163
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:53,000
I have already mentioned to you before.

164
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:55,000
Our belt will be replaced with a harder fabric,

165
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:57,000
which is the Fusible Rigid.

166
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:59,000
The Fusible Rigid fabric used here

167
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:02,000
is very elastic and has a very high tension of the corner line.

168
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:03,000
At the same time,

169
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:05,000
it also has a very high bending strength.

170
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:09,000
This means that it is a fabric that is not easy to bend and stretch.

171
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:11,000
We can see that even the skirt version

172
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:14,000
is a very large version.

173
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:18,000
We can see that it has a very large number of creases in the model.

174
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:19,000
However,

175
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:22,000
the belt version has a very small number of creases.

176
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:24,000
As for the skirt version with a large number of creases,

177
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:27,000
it will definitely drag the belt down.

178
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:31,000
So in order to prevent the skirt from falling down

179
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:33,000
during some running and jumping processes,

180
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:36,000
we must replace the belt with this kind of

181
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:37,000
not easy to stretch,

182
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:39,000
bend strength is relatively high attribute.

183
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:40,000
In addition,

184
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:44,000
we also need to further improve the friction coefficient of this fabric.

185
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:46,000
After improving the friction coefficient,

186
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:48,000
all the sheets that use this fabric attribute,

187
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:50,000
that is to say our belt,

188
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:52,000
it will not be easy to slide,

189
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:54,000
because the friction force becomes too strong,

190
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:56,000
you can imagine that

191
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:58,000
when we have a lot of friction,

192
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:00,000
it is very difficult to separate these two objects.

193
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:01,000
In this way,

194
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:03,000
we can further prevent the skirt from falling down

195
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:07,000
during the following action process.

196
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:09,000
After a short simulation,

197
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:11,000
we can start replacing the virtual model.

198
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:12,000
First,

199
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:14,000
delete the excess virtual model,

200
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:18,000
and then import the FBX file with the action.

201
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:19,000
When importing,

202
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:21,000
everyone should also pay attention to

203
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:23,000
whether the unit here is the unit when we export.

204
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:26,000
After importing the FBX file,

205
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:27,000
we must know that

206
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,000
every new imported file,

207
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:30,000
it is default surface diameter is 3.

208
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:32,000
Here we modify it to 1.

209
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:34,000
Then we simulate it briefly,

210
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:36,000
so that the version is in interaction with this virtual model.

211
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:38,000
Now we can start preparing for recording animation.

212
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:40,000
Click on the small triangle mark at the bottom of the screen,

213
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:42,000
we can open the animation editor.

214
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:44,000
Open the animation editor,

215
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:45,000
we can see that

216
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:47,000
the animation is being recorded.

217
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:48,000
We can see that

218
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:49,000
the animation is being recorded.

219
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:50,000
We can see that

220
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:51,000
the animation is being recorded.

221
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:52,000
We can see that

222
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:53,000
the animation is being recorded.

223
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:55,000
After opening the animation editor,

224
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:56,000
we will pull the progress bar

225
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:58,000
to the first frame of all your actions.

226
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:00,000
If you open the animation editor,

227
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:02,000
it does not reach the starting point,

228
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:03,000
we can see that

229
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:05,000
if you directly click on the simulation,

230
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:07,000
the costume is not worn on the virtual model,

231
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:09,000
and the recording is not stable afterwards.

232
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:11,000
Or you can change the current frame number

233
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:14,000
to the starting point of all your action bars.

234
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:16,000
The starting point here is the 0th frame,

235
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:18,000
so I will put the current frame number

236
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:19,000
to the 0th frame.

237
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:21,000
After modifying the starting point,

238
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:23,000
we increase the quality of the simulation a little bit,

239
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:26,000
here we set the quality of the simulation to 5,

240
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:28,000
which is the finished quality.

241
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:30,000
The higher the quality of the simulation,

242
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:33,000
the higher the precision of the simulation,

243
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:35,000
that is, the more stable it is.

244
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:37,000
The reason why it is stable

245
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:40,000
is because the higher the precision of the simulation,

246
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:42,000
the longer the simulation time

247
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:43,000
you need for each frame,

248
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:46,000
because it needs to be recalculated in the background.

249
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:47,000
So the higher the value,

250
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:48,000
the more precise the simulation,

251
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:50,000
and the time it takes to calculate

252
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:51,000
will increase accordingly.

